  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A notebook can record observations by bed, by date, or with links between both.\", \"decision\": \"How should garden observations be kept useful?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers keep a page for each bed and add dated observations to it. Changes within a bed are easy to follow.\nVolunteers keep a page for each date and list the beds observed that day. Conditions across the garden can be compared at one visit.\nVolunteers record observations on dated cards and file copies under the relevant beds. Both visit-level and bed-level review remain possible."
    }
  ],
